[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbeder/yaml-cpp/issues/comments/134377276","html_url":"https://github.com/jbeder/yaml-cpp/issues/232#issuecomment-134377276","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbeder/yaml-cpp/issues/232","id":134377276,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDEzNDM3NzI3Ng==","user":{"login":"ramoncreager","id":634466,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNDQ2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/634466?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager","html_url":"https://github.com/ramoncreager","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-08-24T20:55:12Z","updated_at":"2015-08-24T20:55:12Z","body":"My apologies if I'm not adding anything new here, but I see the same issue. Is there some work-around to this? It's got me in a bit of a bind. I'm using yaml-cpp as the basis of a key-value store, and It's behind an interface. If there were some way to flush the memory that would work for me.\n\nBy examining the valgrind output of the simple example below and looking at the source I see that `YAML::detail::memory::create_node()` places a `shared_ptr` into a set, but don't see how that `shared_ptr` ever goes out of scope unless that `YAML::detail::memory` object does.\n\nThanks!\n\n```\n  YAML::Node n = YAML::Load(\"{bar: 1, foo: 12345}\");\n  while (1)\n  { \n      int i = 0;\n      n[\"foo\"] = i++;\n  }\n```\n\nMy valgrind output:\n\n==12709== 83,584 bytes in 1,306 blocks are still reachable in loss record 239 of 240\n==12709==    at 0x4A075FC: operator new(unsigned long) (vg_replace_malloc.c:298)\n==12709==    by 0x4CA91C6: YAML::detail::memory::create_node() (in /home/.../lib/libyaml-cpp.so.0.5.2)\n==12709==    by 0x403A4D: YAML::detail::memory_holder::create_node() (memory.h:39)\n==12709==    by 0x4049ED: YAML::Node::Nodestd::string(std::string const&) (impl.h:31)\n==12709==    by 0x4043DD: YAML::convert<int>::encode(int const&) (in /home/.../test)\n==12709==    by 0x405394: void YAML::Node::Assign<int>(int const&) (impl.h:216)\n==12709==    by 0x404CCC: YAML::Node& YAML::Node::operator=<int>(int const&) (impl.h:201)\n==12709==    by 0x403087: main (main.cc:76)\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbeder/yaml-cpp/issues/comments/134377276/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbeder/yaml-cpp/issues/comments/134467500","html_url":"https://github.com/jbeder/yaml-cpp/issues/232#issuecomment-134467500","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbeder/yaml-cpp/issues/232","id":134467500,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDEzNDQ2NzUwMA==","user":{"login":"jbeder","id":1059334,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTkzMzQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1059334?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbeder","html_url":"https://github.com/jbeder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbeder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbeder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbeder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbeder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbeder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbeder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbeder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbeder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbeder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-08-25T03:53:11Z","updated_at":"2015-08-25T03:53:11Z","body":"I suspect (though I haven't verified this) that `YAML::Clone` will strip the excess memory. That is, when you want to \"flush the memory\", clone the node and drop the reference to the original node.\n","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbeder/yaml-cpp/issues/comments/134467500/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbeder/yaml-cpp/issues/comments/134584179","html_url":"https://github.com/jbeder/yaml-cpp/issues/232#issuecomment-134584179","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbeder/yaml-cpp/issues/232","id":134584179,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDEzNDU4NDE3OQ==","user":{"login":"ramoncreager","id":634466,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNDQ2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/634466?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager","html_url":"https://github.com/ramoncreager","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramoncreager/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-08-25T13:23:34Z","updated_at":"2015-08-25T13:23:34Z","body":"Yes, I suspected as much. Here's what I did:\n\n```\n  std::list<YAML::Node> node_list;\n  node_list.push_front(YAML::Load(\"{bar: 1, foo: 0}\"));\n  while (!done)\n  {\n        node_list.front()[\"foo\"] = i++;\n        node_list.push_front(YAML::Clone(node_list.front()));\n        node_list.pop_back();\n  }\n\n  cout << node_list.front() << endl;\n```\n\nAnd indeed, key \"foo\" tracks the increasing value of i, and no memory is lost.\n\nThanks!\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jbeder/yaml-cpp/issues/comments/134584179/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]